{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"451ae9891f6725f72cbd8f16340ce3314b25a347b5fb167318ee573b46400f37","digest":{"component_or_area":"MCP write surface - unlink_tickets adapter","key_entities":["src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py::unlink_tickets","src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py::unlink","rebar.unlink","relation parameter","docs/mcp-reference.md","scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py","tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_unlink_relation.py"],"problem_keywords":["mcp parameter parity","relation selector","unlink operation","incomplete implementation","missing parameter forwarding"],"propositions":["MCP unlink_tickets adapter omits optional relation parameter from both its registered FastMCP signature and its rebar.unlink delegate call","When multiple relations exist between a ticket pair, MCP cannot remove a specific relation and falls back to removing the most-recent edge instead of the requested one","The library, CLI, and documentation already support relation-scoped unlink but MCP diverges due to missing parameter declaration and forwarding in the adapter","The registered FastMCP schema advertises only id1 and id2, preventing callers from expressing which relation to remove when a pair holds multiple edges","Supplying relation=\"blocks\" through MCP currently fails to remove only the blocks edge; omitting relation should preserve documented pair-scoped most-recent behavior"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787910077651826001,"uuid":"6bbb0db4-81b1-4692-90db-cdc6a85a33b4"}